      {
        "id": 2717054509,
        "content": "We need to populate our matchmaking database. We \"register\" users in our system when they \"Sign in with GitHub\" on https://devpool.directory/\r\nI suppose with GraphQL it may be simple to check every issue that is closed as complete with these assignees. \r\n- We need to capture all of the metadata to make it easier to work with later.\r\n- We need to be able to determine the location of the issue, which means organization and repository. We should capture both the names as well as the IDs, in case of renames. \r\n- We need to generate vector embeddings and store the specifications in plain text. \r\nFor now we can work off of a static snapshot of registrants. In the future, we should automatically scrape their completed issues as soon as they register on our site. \r\n[auth.users.json](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18005367/auth.users.json)\r\n[auth.users.csv](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18005368/auth.users.csv)",
